Step 1 — Create New Project
1. Open Visual Studio 2019.
2. Click Create a new project.
3. Select:
ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework)

4. Click Next.
Project Name	StudentCRUD
Framework	.NET Framework 4.7.2

Click Create.
Step 3 — Select MVC
Select:
MVC

Authentication:
No Authentication

Click Create.   
Step 4 — Run the Application
Press:
Ctrl + F5

The default MVC application should open.
Step 5 — Install Entity Framework 6
Open:
Tools
→ NuGet Package Manager
→ Package Manager Console

Run:
Install-Package EntityFramework
Wait until the installation completes.    

Step 6 — Create Student Model
1. Right-click Models.
2. Select:
Add → Class
3. Name it:
Student.cs

4. Add:

using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace StudentCRUD.Models
{
    public class Student
    {
        [Key]
        public int StudentId { get; set; }

        [Required]
        [StringLength(50)]
        public string Name { get; set; }

        [Range(18, 60)]
        public int Age { get; set; }

        [StringLength(50)]
        public string Course { get; set; }
    }
}

   
Step 7 — Create Database Context
1. Right-click Models.
2. Select:
Add → Class

3. Name it:
StudentContext.cs

4. Add:
using System.Data.Entity;

namespace StudentCRUD.Models
{
    public class StudentContext : DbContext
    {
        public StudentContext()
            : base("StudentConnection")
        {
        }

        public DbSet<Student> Students
        {
            get;
            set;
        }
    }
}

Step 8 — Configure Connection String
Open:
Web.config

Inside <configuration>, add:
<connectionStrings>
    <add name="StudentConnection"
         connectionString="Data Source=(LocalDB)\MSSQLLocalDB;Initial Catalog=StudentDB;Integrated Security=True"
         providerName="System.Data.SqlClient"/>
</connectionStrings>

Step 9 — Enable Migrations

Open:
Tools → NuGet Package Manager → Package Manager Console
Run:
Enable-Migrations
if error occur change the entire Web config.

A Migrations folder will be created.
Step 10 — Create Migration
In Package Manager Console, run:
Add-Migration InitialCreate

Step 11 — Create Database
Run:
Update-Database

This creates:
StudentDB
and the:
Studentstable.    

Step 12 — Verify Database
Open:
View
→ SQL Server Object Explorer

Expand:
(localdb)\MSSQLLocalDB
    ↓
StudentDB
    ↓
Tables
    ↓
dbo.Students

Step 13 — Create Controller
1. Right-click Controllers.
2. Select:
Add → Controller

3. Select:
MVC 5 Controller with views, using Entity Framework

4. Click Add.
Step 14 — Configure Controller
Set:
Option	Value
Model Class	Student
Data Context Class	StudentContext
Controller Name	StudentsController


Click Add.
